- hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase type 3 (3alpha-HSD3) and alpha4 GABA-A receptor subunit (22-fold) was observed.", citationComment:"Neurosteroid biosynthetic pathway changes in substantia nigra and caudate nucleus in Parkinson's disease.", citationTitle:"Brain pathology (Zurich, Switzerland); Vol. 20; Iss. 5", annotationSubgraph:["GABA subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Caudate Nucleus"], citationPubDate:"2010-09-01", pmid:"20406233", citationAuthorList:"Sabina Luchetti|Koen Bossers|Giovanni Vanni Frajese|Dick F Swaab", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20406233"}}] AS row
