ssive daytime sleepiness (EDS) (Abbott et al. 2005; Gao J et al. 2011), and autonomic dysfunction (Goldstein 2010) may occur well before the appearance of the classic motor dysfunction of PD.", citationTitle:"Environ Health Perspect. 2013 Nov-Dec;121(11-12):1245-52. doi: 10.1289/ehp.1306967. Epub 2013 Aug 7.", annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"23933572", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"23933572"}}, {start: {_id:1206}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"Accumulating epidemiological and clinical evidence suggests that hyposmia (Ross et al. 2008), constipation (Abbott et al. 2007; Gao X et al. 2011; Savica et al. 2009), depression (Bower et al. 2010; Fang et al. 2010; Ishihara-Paul et al. 2008; Shiba et al. 2000), anxiety (Bower et al. 2010; Ishihara-Paul et al. 2008; Shiba et al. 2000; Weisskopf et al. 2003), rapid eye movement sleep behavior disorder (RBD) (Claassen et al. 2010; Iranzo et al. 2006; Postuma et al. 2009; Schenck et al. 1996), excessive daytime sleepiness (EDS) (Abbott et al. 2005; Gao J et al. 2011), and autonomic dysfunction (Goldstein 2010) may occur well before the appearance of the classic motor dysfunction of PD.", citationTitle:"Environ Health Perspect. 2013 Nov-Dec;121(11-12):1245-52. doi: 10.1289/ehp.1306967. Epub 2013 Aug 7.", annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"23933572", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"23933572"}}, {start: {_id:1207}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"Accumulating epidemiological and clinical evidence suggests that hyposmia (Ross et al. 2008), constipation (Abbott et al. 2007; Gao X et al. 2011; Savica et al. 2009), depression (Bower et al. 2010; Fang et al. 2010; Ishihara-Paul et al. 2008; Shiba et al. 2000), anxiety (Bower et al. 2010; Ishihara-Paul et al. 2008; Shiba et al. 2000; Weisskopf et al. 2003), rapid eye movement sleep behavior disorder (RBD) (Claassen et al. 2010; Iranzo et al. 2006; Postuma et al. 2009; Schenck et al. 1996), excessive daytime sleepiness (EDS) (Abbott et al. 2005; Gao J et al. 2011), and autonomic dysfunction (Goldstein 2010) may occur well before the appearance of the classic motor dysfunction of PD.", citationTitle:"Environ Health Perspect. 2013 Nov-Dec;121(11-12):1245-52. doi: 10.1289/ehp.1306967. Epub 2013 Aug 7.", annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"23933572", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"23933572"}}, {start: {_id:612}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"Among RBD patients, Postuma et al. (2012b) documented multiple motor abnormalities on average 6â€šÃ„Ã¬8 years prior to PD diagnosis, including voice and face akinesia, rigidity, abnormal gait, limb bradykinesia.", citationTitle:"Environ Health Perspect. 2013 Nov-Dec;121(11-12):1245-52. doi: 10.1289/ehp.1306967. Epub 2013 Aug 7.", annotationSubgraph:["Synuclein subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease", "REM Sleep Behavior Disorder"], pmid:"23933572", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"23933572"}}, {start: {_id:1208}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"Among RBD patients, Postuma et al. (2012b) documented multiple motor abnormalities on average 6â€šÃ„Ã¬8 years prior to PD diagnosis, including voice and face akinesia, rigidity, abnormal gait, limb bradykinesia.", citationTitle:"Environ Health Perspect. 2013 Nov-Dec;121(11-12):1245-52. doi: 10.1289/ehp.1306967. Epub 2013 Aug 7.", annotationSubgraph:["Synuclein subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease", "REM Sleep Behavior Disorder"], pmid:"23933572", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"23933572"}}, {start: {_id:1179}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"In PD patients, but not in controls, cortical atrophy in olfactory- related brain regions correlated specifically with olfactory dysfunction. Positive correlations between olfactory performance and gray matter volume were observed in the right piriform cortex in early PD patients and in the right amygdala in moderately advanced patients. The results provided first evidence that olfactory dysfunction in PD is related to atrophy in olfactory-eloquent regions of the limbic and paralimbic cortex. In addition, olfactory-correlated atrophy in these brain regions is consistent with the assumption that olfactory impairment as an early symptom of PD is likely to be associated with extranigral pathology.", citationTitle:"J Neurosci. 2009 Dec 9;29(49):15410-3. doi: 10.1523/JNEUROSCI.1909-09.2009.", annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"20007465", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20007465"}}, {start: {_id:719}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"mitochondrial dysfunction as a contributor to the molecular pathogenesis of neurodegenerative diseases such as Parkinson's disease.", citationTitle:"Dev Cell. 2012 Feb 14;22(2):320-33. doi: 10.1016/j.devcel.2011.12.014. Epub 2012 Jan 25.", annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"22280891", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22280891"}}, {start: {_id:16}, end: {_id:1695}, properties:{evidence:"PD is a common progressive neurodegenerative movement disorder characterized by postural instability, rigidity, tremor and bradykinesia", citationTitle:"EMBO Mol Med. 2009 May;1(2):99-111. doi: 10.1002/emmm.200900006.", annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"20049710", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20049710"}}, {start: {_id:16}, end: {_id:1696}, properties:{evidence:"PD is a common progressive neurodegenerative movement disorder characterized by postural instability, rigidity, tremor and bradykinesia", citationTitle:"EMBO Mol Med. 2009 May;1(2):99-111. doi: 10.1002/emmm.200900006.", annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"20049710", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20049710"}}, {start: {_id:719}, end: {_id:550}, properties:{evidence:"Mitochondria play essential roles in many aspects of biology, and their dysfunction has been linked to diverse diseases.", citationTitle:"Cell Metab. 2015 Jan 6;21(1):95-108. doi: 10.1016/j.cmet.2014.12.007.", annotationMeshdisease:["Neurodegenerative Diseases"], pmid:"25565208", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"25565208"}}, {start: {_id:719}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"Mitochondrial dysfunction is a hallmark of both idiopathic and familial Parkinson's disease (PD).", citationTitle:"Biochem Soc Trans. 2015 Apr;43(2):297-301. doi: 10.1042/BST20150008.", annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"25849933", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"25849933"}}, {start: {_id:1914}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"Our study supports the notion that parkin has a role in the interorganellar crosstalk between the ER and mitochondria to promote cell survival under stress, suggesting that both ER and mitochondrial stress can contribute to the pathogenesis of Parkinsonâ€™s disease.", citationTitle:"Cell Death Differ. 2011 May;18(5):769-82. doi: 10.1038/cdd.2010.142. Epub 2010 Nov 26.", annotationSubgraph:["Ubiquitin subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Mitochondria"], pmid:"21113145", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"21113145"}}, {start: {_id:719}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"Mitochondrial dysfunction and endoplasmic reticulum (ER) stress contribute to the pathogenesis of Parkinson disease (PD)", citationTitle:"Biochim Biophys Acta. 2013 Apr;1832(4):495-508. doi: 10.1016/j.bbadis.2013.01.004. Epub 2013 Jan 9.", annotationSubgraph:["Ubiquitin subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"23313576", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"23313576"}}] AS row
MATCH (start:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row.start._id})
MATCH (end:`UNIQUE IMPORT LABEL`{`UNIQUE IMPORT ID`: row.end._id})
CREATE (start)-[r:INCREASES]->(end) SET r += row.properties;
UNWIND [{start: {_id:1004}, end: {_id:872}, properties:{}}, {start: {_id:1008}, end: {_id:872}, properties:{}}, {start: {_id:1017}, end: {_id:872}, properties:{}}, {start: {_id:1021}, end: {_id:1005}, properties:{}}] AS row
