UNWIND [{start: {_id:916}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"This work revealed notable differences in phosphorylation patterns between PD and other tauopathies. For instance, S202, T205, S262, S409 are hyperphosphorylated in AD and DLB, but are unchanged in PD, while others such as T181, S184, S195, S198, S237, S400 are hyperphosphorylated in all three, AD, DLB, and PD.", citationTitle:"Front Genet. 2014 Nov 7;5:382. doi: 10.3389/fgene.2014.00382. eCollection 2014", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"25426138", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"25426138"}}, {start: {_id:918}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"This work revealed notable differences in phosphorylation patterns between PD and other tauopathies. For instance, S202, T205, S262, S409 are hyperphosphorylated in AD and DLB, but are unchanged in PD, while others such as T181, S184, S195, S198, S237, S400 are hyperphosphorylated in all three, AD, DLB, and PD.", citationTitle:"Front Genet. 2014 Nov 7;5:382. doi: 10.3389/fgene.2014.00382. eCollection 2014", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"25426138", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"25426138"}}, {start: {_id:920}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"This work revealed notable differences in phosphorylation patterns between PD and other tauopathies. For instance, S202, T205, S262, S409 are hyperphosphorylated in AD and DLB, but are unchanged in PD, while others such as T181, S184, S195, S198, S237, S400 are hyperphosphorylated in all three, AD, DLB, and PD.", citationTitle:"Front Genet. 2014 Nov 7;5:382. doi: 10.3389/fgene.2014.00382. eCollection 2014", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"25426138", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"25426138"}}, {start: {_id:43}, end: {_id:929}, properties:{evidence:"Dopa decarboxylase (DDC) catalyses the synthesis of both dopamine and serotonin as well as trace amines suggested to possess neuromodulating capabilities. We have previously reported evidence suggesting an association between DDC and bipolar affective disorder (BPAD) [BâˆšÃ‰Â¬âˆ�rglum et al., 1999].", citationTitle:"Am J Med Genet B Neuropsychiatr Genet. 2003 Feb;117B(1):18-22.", annotationSubgraph:["Dopaminergic subgraph"], pmid:"12555230", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"12555230"}}, {start: {_id:962}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{annotationBrco:["Spinal motor neuron"], evidence:"Haplotype results indicate that the minor allele of the rs4739217 is a risk factor for TD (permuted allelic p = 0.074). Age was also a risk factor for TD in our sample (p = 0.0001). Taken together, our findings suggest that GFRA2 genetic variants and age may play a role in TD susceptibility, but further work is required to confirm these findings", citationTitle:"Psychopharmacology (Berl). 2010 Jun;210(3):347-54. doi: 10.1007/s00213-010-1829-4. Epub 2010 Apr 6.", annotationSubgraph:["Neurotrophic subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["9606"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Dopaminergic Neurons"], pmid:"20369355", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20369355"}}, {start: {_id:994}, end: {_id:995}, properties:{evidence:"Alzheimer's disease (AD) is the most common neurodegenerative disease, and is clinically characterized by cognitive disturbances and the accumulation of the amyloid âˆšÃ©Â¬â‰¤ (AâˆšÃ©Â¬â‰¤) peptides in plaques in the brain. Recent studies have shown the links between AD and the immediate-early gene Arc (activity-regulated cytoskeleton- associated protein), involved in synaptic plasticity and memory consolidation. For example, AD mouse models show a decreased expression of Arc mRNA in the brain.", citationTitle:"J Neural Transm. 2012 Jul;119(7):833-42. doi: 10.1007/s00702-012-0823-x. Epub 2012 May 25.", annotationSubgraph:["Regulation of cytoskeleton subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["9606"], annotationMeshdisease:["Alzheimer Disease"], pmid:"22622366", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22622366"}}, {start: {_id:1012}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"Apolipoprotein E (APOE) seems to be the most important mediator of this recycling process, but also other lipoproteins have been implicated, e.g. apolipoproteins J and D. The thrifty nature of cholesterol homeostasis in the brain is most probably a consequence of the low rate of de novo cholesterol synthesis in the adult brain, most of which is believed to occur in glial cells. Neurons are believed to have a very low rate of cholesterol synthesis and meet their cholesterol requirements via uptake of cholesterol carried in APOE- containing lipoproteins secreted from glial cells ( Pfrieger, 2003). Accumulating epidemiological and molecular evidence indicates that there is a clear link between cholesterol turnover and neurodegenerative diseases âˆšÂ¢â€šÃ‡Â¨â€šÃ„Ãº hypercholesterolemia per-se is an important risk factor for AlzheimerâˆšÂ¢â€šÃ‡Â¨â€šÃ‘Â¢s disease (AD) and ParkinsonâˆšÂ¢â€šÃ‡Â¨â€šÃ‘Â¢s disease and the presence of an APOE âˆšÃ©Â¬Âµ4 allele is the most well described genetic risk factor for late onset AD (LOAD).", citationTitle:"Mol Aspects Med. 2009 Jun;30(3):171-9. doi: 10.1016/j.mam.2009.02.001. Epub 2009 Feb 25.", annotationSubgraph:["APOE subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["10116"], pmid:"19248803", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"19248803"}}, {start: {_id:1037}, end: {_id:1038}, properties:{evidence:"Estrogen receptors (ERÅ’Â± and ERÅ’â‰¤) mediate the neuroprotection of estrogens against MPTP-induced striatal dopamine (DA) depletion. Pain is an important and distressing symptom in Parkinson's disease (PD). Voltage-gated sodium channels in sensory neurons are involved in the development of neuropathic pain.The MPTP-induced up-regulation of Nav1.1 and Nav1.9, down-regulation of Nav1.6 in DRG neurons may be through ERÅ’â‰¤, up-regulation of Nav1.7 and down-regulation of Nav1.8 are dependent on both ERÅ’Â± and ERÅ’â‰¤.", citationTitle:"Endocrine. 2012 Aug;42(1):118-24. doi: 10.1007/s12020-012-9637-8. Epub 2012 Feb 28.", annotationSubgraph:["Estrogen subgraph", "Calcium-dependent signal transduction"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"22371119", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22371119"}}, {start: {_id:1050}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"These data imply an involvement of pregnane steroids and changes in GABAergic neurotransmission in the neurodegenerative process and suggest that neurosteroids may deserve further investigation as potential therapeutic agents in PD", citationTitle:"Brain Pathol. 2010 Sep;20(5):945-51. doi: 10.1111/j.1750-3639.2010.00396.x. Epub 2010 Mar 19.", annotationSubgraph:["GABA subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Substantia Nigra"], pmid:"20406233", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20406233"}}, {start: {_id:1055}, end: {_id:1056}, properties:{evidence:"Oligophrenin-1 encodes a rhoGAP protein involved in X-linked mental retardation.", citationTitle:"Nature. 1998 Apr 30;392(6679):923-6.", annotationSubgraph:["Regulation of cytoskeleton subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Mental Retardation, X-Linked"], pmid:"9582072", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"9582072"}}, {start: {_id:1072}, end: {_id:1070}, properties:{evidence:"Charcot-Marie-Tooth disease type 4B is caused by mutations in the genes encoding either the lipid phosphatase myotubularin-related protein-2 (MTMR2) or its regulatory binding partner MTMR13/SBF2.", citationComment:"The CMT4B disease-causing proteins MTMR2 and MTMR13/SBF2 regulate AKT signalling.", citationTitle:"Journal of cellular and molecular medicine; Vol. 15; Iss. 2", annotationSubgraph:["Phosphatidylinositol 3 subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Charcot-Marie-Tooth Disease"], citationPubDate:"2011-02-01", pmid:"19912440", citationAuthorList:"Philipp Berger|Kristian Tersar|Kurt Ballmer-Hofer|Ueli Suter", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"19912440"}}, {start: {_id:1122}, end: {_id:1123}, properties:{evidence:"Resistin is a polypeptide hormone that was reported to be associated with insulin resistance, inflammation and risk of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.", citationTitle:"Hum Mol Genet. 2012 Nov 1;21(21):4774-80. doi: 10.1093/hmg/dds300. Epub 2012 Jul 26.", annotationSubgraph:["Insulin signal transduction"], annotationMeshdisease:["Cardiovascular Diseases", "Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2"], pmid:"22843503", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22843503"}}, {start: {_id:1122}, end: {_id:1124}, properties:{evidence:"Resistin is a polypeptide hormone that was reported to be associated with insulin resistance, inflammation and risk of type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease.", citationTitle:"Hum Mol Genet. 2012 Nov 1;21(21):4774-80. doi: 10.1093/hmg/dds300. Epub 2012 Jul 26.", annotationSubgraph:["Insulin signal transduction"], annotationMeshdisease:["Cardiovascular Diseases", "Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2"], pmid:"22843503", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22843503"}}, {start: {_id:1177}, end: {_id:1170}, properties:{evidence:"DYT-1 gene dystonic tremor presenting as a scan without evidence of dopaminergic deficit", citationTitle:"Mov Disord. 2012 Sep 15;27(11):1469. ", annotationSubgraph:["Chaperone subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Dystonic Disorders", "Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"22976004", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22976004"}}, {start: {_id:419}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{annotationPdstage:["Idiopathic_PD"], evidence:"The human tau gene, which promotes assembly of neuronal microtubules, has been associated with several rare neurologic diseases that clinically include parkinsonian features. We recently observed linkage in idiopathic Parkinson disease (PD) to a region on chromosome 17q21 that contains the tau gene.", citationTitle:"JAMA. 2001 Nov 14;286(18):2245-50.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["9606"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"11710889", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"11710889"}}, {start: {_id:1315}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{annotationPdstage:["Idiopathic_PD"], evidence:"we tested 5 single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs) within the tau gene for association with PD .Three SNPs (3, 9i, and 11) showed significant association with PD(Table1)", citationTitle:"JAMA. 2001 Nov 14;286(18):2245-50.", annotationSubgraph:["Tau protein subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["9606"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"11710889", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"11710889"}}, {start: {_id:1469}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"The R275W polymorphism in Parkin and the G411S polymorphism in PINK1 have only been identified as heterozygous polymorphisms in cases of Parkinson disease", citationTitle:"PLoS Biol. 2010 Jan 26;8(1):e1000298. doi: 10.1371/journal.pbio.1000298.", annotationSubgraph:["Ubiquitin subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Mitochondria"], pmid:"20126261", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20126261"}}, {start: {_id:1471}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"The R275W polymorphism in Parkin and the G411S polymorphism in PINK1 have only been identified as heterozygous polymorphisms in cases of Parkinson disease", citationTitle:"PLoS Biol. 2010 Jan 26;8(1):e1000298. doi: 10.1371/journal.pbio.1000298.", annotationSubgraph:["PINK1 subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Mitochondria"], pmid:"20126261", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"20126261"}}, {start: {_id:1480}, end: {_id:16}, properties:{evidence:"we assessed the complex assembly of PINK1 PD patient mutants A168P, H271Q and G309D using the in vitro import assay", citationTitle:"Dev Cell. 2012 Feb 14;22(2):320-33. doi: 10.1016/j.devcel.2011.12.014. Epub 2012 Jan 25.", annotationSubgraph:["PINK1 subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"22280891", citationType:"Pu