.1126/science.1218632. Epub 2012 May 10.", annotationSubgraph:["Cholesterol metabolism subgraph", "PINK1 subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["7227"], pmid:"22582012", annotationDisease:["Parkinson's disease"], citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22582012"}}, {start: {_id:1747}, end: {_id:221}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"Thus, Heix is a dosage-sensitive modifier of pink1.", citationTitle:"Science. 2012 Jun 8;336(6086):1306-10. doi: 10.1126/science.1218632. Epub 2012 May 10.", annotationSubgraph:["Cholesterol metabolism subgraph", "PINK1 subgraph"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Mitochondria"], pmid:"22582012", annotationDisease:["Parkinson's disease"], citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22582012"}}, {start: {_id:1768}, end: {_id:601}, properties:{evidence:"HSD17B10 is also thought to have a role in adult- onset neurodegenerative disorders, such as Alzheimerâ€™s disease, in which it may mediate amyloid Î²-driven mitochondrial toxicity,25,29,30 and PD, in which it is downregulated in the ventral midbrain.", citationTitle:"Cell Death Differ. 2015 Oct;22(10):1563-76. doi: 10.1038/cdd.2014.224. Epub 2015 Jan 16.", annotationSubgraph:["Amyloidogenic subgraph", "Mitochondrial subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Alzheimer Disease"], pmid:"25591737", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"25591737"}}, {start: {_id:1768}, end: {_id:1805}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"Here, we provide evidence that Parkin increases the mitochondrial availability of HSD17B10 in a ubiquitin-dependent manner", citationTitle:"Cell Death Differ. 2015 Oct;22(10):1563-76. doi: 10.1038/cdd.2014.224. Epub 2015 Jan 16.", annotationSubgraph:["Mitochondrial subgraph"], annotationMeshanatomy:["Mitochondria"], pmid:"25591737", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"25591737"}}, {start: {_id:1768}, end: {_id:271}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"Our results suggest that the maintenance of appropriate HSD17B10 l