"PubMed", citationRef:"25565208"}}, {start: {_id:1850}, end: {_id:1838}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"We hypothesize that ubiquitination of Glo alters the structure of the repressor complexes and their binding to nRCC mRNAs.", citationTitle:"Cell Metab. 2015 Jan 6;21(1):95-108. doi: 10.1016/j.cmet.2014.12.007.", annotationSubgraph:["Pre-translational events"], pmid:"25565208", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"25565208"}}, {start: {_id:221}, end: {_id:1829}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"Although PINK1 can also interact with the TOM complex, it is unlikely that the effect of PINK1/Parkin on mRNA translation is mediated by TOM, since the interaction between PINK1 and TOM is transient and weaker than the interaction between PINK1 and the translation machinery, and a direct role for TOM in mRNA translation is not known.", citationTitle:"Cell Metab. 2015 Jan 6;21(1):95-108. doi: 10.1016/j.cmet.2014.12.007.", annotationSubgraph:["PINK1 subgraph"], pmid:"25565208", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"25565208"}}, {start: {_id:1881}, end: {_id:1878}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"Taken together, these findings indicate that CHCHD4 plays a central role in the biogenesis of specific respiratory chain complexes.", citationTitle:"Mol Cell. 2015 Jun 18;58(6):1001-14. doi: 10.1016/j.molcel.2015.04.020. Epub 2015 May 21.", annotationSubgraph:["Mitochondrial subgraph", "Chaperone subgraph"], pmid:"26004228", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"26004228"}}, {start: {_id:1881}, end: {_id:1880}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"Taken together, these findings indicate that CHCHD4 plays a central role in the biogenesis of specific respiratory chain complexes.", citationTitle:"Mol Cell. 2015 Jun 18;58(6):1001-14. doi: 10.1016/j.molcel.2015.04.020. Epub 2015 May 21.", annotationSubgraph:["Mitochondrial subgraph", "Chaperone subgraph"], pmid:"26004228", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"26004228"}}, {start: {_id:1881}, end: {_id:1836}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"Taken together, these findings indicate that CHCHD4 plays a central role in the biogenesis of specific respiratory chain complexes.", citationTitle:"Mol Cell. 2015 Jun 18;58(6):1001-14. doi: 10.1016/j.molcel.2015.04.020. Epub 2015 May 21.", annotationSubgraph:["Mitochondrial subgraph", "Chaperone subgraph"], pmid:"26004228", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"26004228"}}, {start: {_id:1883}, end: {_id:1906}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"The N-terminal, 27-amino-acid-long fragment of CHCHD4 was necessary and sufficient for it to interact with AIF, while the redox function of CHCHD4 was irrelevant to the CHCHD4/AIF interaction.", citationTitle:"Mol Cell. 2015 Jun 18;58(6):1001-14. doi: 10.1016/j.molcel.2015.04.020. Epub 2015 May 21.", annotationSubgraph:["Apoptosis signaling subgraph", "Chaperone subgraph"], pmid:"26004228", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"26004228"}}, {start: {_id:1883}, end: {_id:1906}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"Future co-crystallization of these interactors may confirm the hypothesis that the N terminus of CHCHD4 acquires a defined structure as it binds to AIF.", citationTitle:"Mol Cell. 2015 Jun 18;58(6):1001-14. doi: 10.1016/j.molcel.2015.04.020. Epub 2015 May 21.", annotationSubgraph:["Apoptosis signaling subgraph", "Chaperone subgraph"], pmid:"26004228", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"26004228"}}] AS row
