and secretion of interleukin 1Beta (IL-1Beta) and IL-18.", citationTitle:"Nat Immunol. 2011 Mar;12(3):222-30. doi: 10.1038/ni.1980. Epub 2010 Dec 12.", annotationSubgraph:["Caspase subgraph", "MAPK subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"21151103", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"21151103"}}, {start: {_id:556}, end: {_id:768}, properties:{evidence:"Autophagy, a cellular process for organelle and protein turnover, regulates innate immune responses. Here we demonstrate that depletion of the autophagic proteins LC3B and beclin 1 enhanced the activation of caspase-1 and secretion of interleukin 1Beta (IL-1Beta) and IL-18.", citationTitle:"Nat Immunol. 2011 Mar;12(3):222-30. doi: 10.1038/ni.1980. Epub 2010 Dec 12.", annotationSubgraph:["Caspase subgraph", "Autophagy signaling subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Parkinson Disease"], pmid:"21151103", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"21151103"}}, {start: {_id:1976}, end: {_id:768}, properties:{annotationCondition:["Normal Healthy State"], evidence:"LC3B-deficient mice produced more caspase-1-dependent cytokines in two sepsis models and were susceptible to LPS-induced mortality. Our study suggests that autophagic proteins regulate NALP3-dependent inflammation by preserving mitochondrial integrity.", citationTitle:"Nat Immunol. 2011 Mar;12(3):222-30. doi: 10.1038/ni.1980. Epub 2010 Dec 12.", annotationSubgraph:["Caspase subgraph", "MAPK subgraph"], pmid:"21151103", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"21151103"}}, {start: {_id:1380}, end: {_id:2144}, properties:{evidence:"In mouse macrophages, TREM-2 is induced by IL-4 and is down-regulated by IFN-gamma or LPS XREF_BIBR.", annotationSubgraph:["Interferon signaling subgraph", "Inflammatory response subgraph"], annotationSpecies:["10090"], annotationConfidence:["Very High"], pmid:"18446208", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"18446208"}}, {start: {_id:509}, end: {_id:89}, properties:{evidence:"These experiments indicate that TNF-alpha promotes IGF-1 receptor resistance in neurons and inhibits the ability of the IGF-I receptor to tyrosine phosphorylate the IRS-2 docking molecule and to subsequently activate the critical downstream enzyme phospha", annotationSubgraph:["Tumor necrosis factor subgraph", "Insulin signal transduction"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"10449788", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"10449788"}}, {start: {_id:2202}, end: {_id:89}, properties:{evidence:"Of the naturally occurring variations in WT1 structure, only the presence of a three-amino acid KTS insert in the zinc finger domain introduced by alternative splicing of exon 9 had a significant effect on WT1 repression of IGF-I receptor promoter activit", annotationSubgraph:["Insulin signal transduction"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"10499530", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"10499530"}}, {start: {_id:56}, end: {_id:2220}, properties:{evidence:"These findings suggest that a reduction in the levels of IGF-1R induces a defective glandular homeostasis in the submandibular gland epithelial cells and triggers EAS.", annotationSubgraph:["Insulin signal transduction"], annotationConfidence:["Very High"], pmid:"11693172", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"11693172"}}, {start: {_id:2256}, end: {_id:2257}, properties:{evidence:"Rasagiline is a second-generation MAO-B inhibitor that selectively and irreversibly inhibits brain MAO-B, specifically designed for the treatment of PD.", annotationSubgraph:["Dopaminergic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"21935322", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"21935322"}}, {start: {_id:138}, end: {_id:2259}, properties:{evidence:"MAO-B overexpression inhibited Bcl-2 induction by rasagiline and befloxatone, but did not affect that by (-) deprenyl, suggesting the different mechanisms behind Bcl-2 gene induction by these MAO-B inhibitors.", annotationSubgraph:["Dopaminergic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["High"], pmid:"22065207", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22065207"}}, {start: {_id:2264}, end: {_id:2257}, properties:{evidence:"This property of selegiline, together with observation that the basal ganglia of human brain possessed predominantly MAO-B that could metabolize dopamine led us to initiate a pilot study with selegiline in Parkinson 's disease.", annotationSubgraph:["Dopaminergic subgraph"], annotationConfidence:["Very High"], pmid:"23585716", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"23585716"}}] AS row
