l, best represented by SNP rs3931020 (P = 6.37 âˆšÃ³ 10(-12)) and SNP rs13144478 (P = 6.19 âˆšÃ³ 10(-18)), respectively.", citationTitle:"Hum Mol Genet. 2012 Nov 1;21(21):4774-80. doi: 10.1093/hmg/dds300. Epub 2012 Jul 26.", annotationSubgraph:["Energy metabolic subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2"], pmid:"22843503", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22843503"}}, {start: {_id:1127}, end: {_id:1126}, properties:{evidence:"We confirmed the association with a previously known locus, the RETN gene (19p13.2), and identified two novel loci near the TYW3/CRYZ gene (1p31) and the NDST4 gene (4q25), associated with resistin levels at a genome-wide significant level, best represented by SNP rs3931020 (P = 6.37 âˆšÃ³ 10(-12)) and SNP rs13144478 (P = 6.19 âˆšÃ³ 10(-18)), respectively.", citationTitle:"Hum Mol Genet. 2012 Nov 1;21(21):4774-80. doi: 10.1093/hmg/dds300. Epub 2012 Jul 26.", annotationSubgraph:["Energy metabolic subgraph", "Insulin signal transduction"], annotationMeshdisease:["Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2"], pmid:"22843503", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22843503"}}, {start: {_id:148}, end: {_id:1128}, properties:{evidence:"We confirmed the association with a previously known locus, the RETN gene (19p13.2), and identified two novel loci near the TYW3/CRYZ gene (1p31) and the NDST4 gene (4q25), associated with resistin levels at a genome-wide significant level, best represented by SNP rs3931020 (P = 6.37 âˆšÃ³ 10(-12)) and SNP rs13144478 (P = 6.19 âˆšÃ³ 10(-18)), respectively.", citationTitle:"Hum Mol Genet. 2012 Nov 1;21(21):4774-80. doi: 10.1093/hmg/dds300. Epub 2012 Jul 26.", annotationSubgraph:["Disaccharide metabolism subgraph"], annotationMeshdisease:["Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2"], pmid:"22843503", citationType:"PubMed", citationRef:"22843503"}}, {start: {_id:1138}, end: {_id:158}, properties:{evidence:"In the present study, we examined whether interleukin-10 (IL-10, 1082G/A), interleukin-17A (IL-17A) rs8193036, rs2275913 and inte